//? Title: Tonelli-Shanks: actual prime-field two-adic refinements
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A modular square root needs a solvability test and, in the general case,
progressively smaller two-adic error order. Actual candidate tests and
refinement square chains retain the original examples and residue folding
modulo101.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Validate p as a prime over the complete uint64 range before any shortcut. For
nonzero n, Euler criterion rejects nonresidues. If p mod4=3 use n^((p+1)/4).
Otherwise p-1=Q*2^S with Q odd; choose the first sequential nonresidue z and
initialize c=z^Q,t=n^Q,R=n^((Q+1)/2),M=S. Find least i with t^(2^i)=1, use
b=c^(2^(M-i-1)), update R<-R*b,t<-t*b^2,c<-b^2,M<-i modulo p. M strictly
decreases. Exact unsigned128 products support full-width moduli. Sequential
nonresidue search and deterministic primality validation have their own cost;
the root-kernel product counter excludes validation and is not an unconditional
complete O(log^2 p) claim.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tonelli_shanks_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/tonelli_shanks.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::tonelli_shanks_trace(10, 13);
    std::print("Actual nmodp {}, Q {}, S {}, chosen nonresidue {}; Euler test {}.\n\n| actual M before | i " "| actual tested t squares | b | c after | t after | R after |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               r.reduced, r.odd_part, r.twos, r.nonresidue, r.euler);
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | `{}` | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.M_before, s.i,
                   s.squares, s.b, s.c_after, s.t_after, s.root_after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual10 modulo validated prime13");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual two-adic refinements",
                                     r.refinements));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual smaller root {}", r.result.root));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/tonelli_shanks_tiny.svg");
}
```
