> API and interpretation

Zero has a single distinct root, as does the nonzero residue modulo2; nonzero
odd-prime residues have complementary distinct roots. The returned
representative is the smaller one. Full uint64 modular arithmetic does not imply
constant-time cryptographic behavior. Auxiliary/product/history exhaustion
throws rather than reporting a mathematical nonresidue.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- Shanks, Five Number-theoretic Algorithms, Manitoba Conference on Numerical
  Mathematics (1973),51-70

